# Discord Bot Engineering & Real-Time API Architecture

This skill provides architectural standards, best practices, and operational patterns for developing, deploying, and maintaining production-grade Discord bots across Python (`discord.py` 2.x) and TypeScript (`discord.js` v14+ / `sapphire`).

---

## 1. Modern Discord API v10 Architecture

```text
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                       Discord Gateway                       │
│              (WebSocket wss://gateway.discord.gg)           │
└──────────────┬──────────────────────────────▲───────────────┘
               │ Dispatch Events              │ Heartbeats / Voice
               ▼                              │
┌──────────────────────────────┐ ┌────────────┴───────────────┐
│     Client Gateway Manager   │ │     HTTP Interaction API   │
│  (Opus Voice / State Caches) │ │  (Slash Commands & Modals) │
└──────────────┬───────────────┘ └────────────▲───────────────┘
               │                              │
               ▼                              │
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────┐
│                Application Bot Logic                        │
│   (Commands, Cogs/Subcommands, UI Components, Redis State)  │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Gateway WebSocket vs HTTP Interactions
* **Gateway WebSocket (`discord.py` / `discord.js` standard):**
  Required for bot state caching, real-time message listening, member presence, voice channel streaming, and interactive experiences.
* **HTTP-Only Interactions (Serverless / Webhooks):**
  Receives slash commands via POST requests without maintaining an active WebSocket connection. Requires verifying the `X-Signature-Ed25519` and `X-Signature-Timestamp` headers using the bot's Public Key. Returns synchronous interaction responses within **3,000ms**.

